{title: For God Alone My Soul Waits}
{subtitle: Psalms 62:2}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 69}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] | [Abmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]For God a[Eb]lone my soul waits in [Cm]silence
From him comes [Abmaj7]my salvation
He alone is my [Eb]rock and my sal[Bb]vation
My [Ab]fortress, I [Bb]shall not be shaken
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Pour out your [Bb]heart before him
[Cm]God is a re[Abmaj7]fuge for us [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
For God alone, O my soul, wait in [Cm]silence
For my hope is from [Ab]him
Trust in him at all [Bb]times, O people
[Ab]God is a re[Bb]fuge for [Eb]us
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Pour out your [Bb]heart before him
[Cm]God is a re[Abmaj7]fuge for us
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Eb] | [Bb] | [Cm] | [Abmaj7] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
For God alone
{end_of_verse}
